ANSWER1. Storage Management :
50 GB storage is divided into separate partitions for OS, logs, user files and applications.
Log rotation prevents logs from exceeding 10 GB and protects critical services.
CODE:
#include <stdio.h>
int main() {
    int total = 50, logs = 8;
    printf("Total Storage: %d GB\n", total);
    printf("Log Partition: %d GB\n", logs);
    printf("Log Rotation: Enabled\n");
    return 0;
}
OUTPUT:
Total Storage: 50 GB
Log Partition: 8 GB
Log Rotation: Enabled

