ANSWER4.Faulty Process Management :
The faulty process is identified by CPU usage. Its priority can be reduced or the process can be terminated if necessary.
CODE:
#include <stdio.h>
int main() {
    int cpu;
    printf("Enter CPU usage: ");
    scanf("%d", &cpu);
    if(cpu >= 90)
        printf("Faulty process detected\n");
    else
        printf("Process is normal\n");
    return 0;
}
OUTPUT:
Enter CPU usage: 90
Faulty process detected

ANSWER5.VM RAM Allocation :
The host requires 4 GB and each of the 5 VMs requires 2 GB.
Thus, 14 GB is allocated and 2 GB is kept as reserve.
CODE:
#include <stdio.h>
int main() {
    int i;
    printf("Host RAM: 4 GB\n");
    for(i = 1; i <= 5; i++)
        printf("VM%d RAM: 2 GB\n", i);
    printf("Reserved RAM: 2 GB\n");
    return 0;
}
OUTPUT:
Host RAM: 4 GB
VM1 RAM: 2 GB
VM2 RAM: 2 GB
VM3 RAM: 2 GB
VM4 RAM: 2 GB
VM5 RAM: 2 GB
Reserved RAM: 2 GB
